  "limitations": [
    "Not reachability: the harness calls the stub directly. That a remote caller can reach this stub over real IPC, and under which ability registration and permission state, is not established here and stays an EvidenceObligation.",
    "The interface token methods are supplied by a shim over the real Parcel; the shim forwards to WriteString16/ReadString16 and adds no policy.",
    "MessageHandler::SendMessage records the call instead of dispatching it; the recording is the observable.",
    "poc_compat.h supplies the using-directive for ErrorCode enumerators, which the historical header set does not expose unqualified; it changes no behaviour."
  ],
  "reachability": {
    "status": "partial",
    "summary": "The service exports the stub itself: Platform::SetPlatform constructs it and passes it as the argument of IPlatformApi::registerCallback, a pure virtual on an IRemoteBroker interface whose proxy marshals the object with WriteRemoteObject. A peer that holds that handle reaches OnRemoteRequest with a caller-chosen transaction code and payload, which is why an interface-descriptor check is the relevant defence. Whether an unprivileged or unrelated process can obtain the handle, and what identity the peer has, is NOT established here.",
    "relations": [
      {
        "kind": "stub_is_constructed_in_the_service",
        "path": "services/src/platform.cpp",
        "commit": "e663b47013d534a56165ab7467fbb3e14bf7172b",
        "sha256": "7ebe67fc4bc2c51e149a79f486c8ddea792d4b590cc22045992ce702167d31f4",
        "line": 25,
        "evidence": "sptr < IPlatformCallback > cb = new PlatformCallbackStub();",
        "establishes": "the service process constructs the very stub object this PoC calls, so the target is a real product object rather than a test double",
        "does_not_establish": "that any process other than the service can obtain it"
      },
      {
        "kind": "stub_is_passed_to_a_remote_interface_call",
        "path": "services/src/platform.cpp",
        "commit": "e663b47013d534a56165ab7467fbb3e14bf7172b",
        "sha256": "7ebe67fc4bc2c51e149a79f486c8ddea792d4b590cc22045992ce702167d31f4",
        "line": 26,
        "evidence": "this->platformApi->registerCallback(cb);",
        "establishes": "the stub is handed to a call on IPlatformApi, an interface the service talks to over IPC, rather than kept local",
        "does_not_establish": "which process implements IPlatformApi at this call site, nor the permission or registration gate on that call"
      },
      {
        "kind": "register_callback_is_an_ipc_transaction",
        "path": "services/include/i_platform_api.h",
        "commit": "e663b47013d534a56165ab7467fbb3e14bf7172b",
        "sha256": "c2985b3853e054da928cea51b12d7c7e1ddaef8fec613f4538e32ce1cb77a196",
        "line": 48,
        "evidence": "virtual int32_t registerCallback(const sptr<IPlatformCallback>& cb) = 0;",
        "establishes": "registerCallback is a pure virtual on an IRemoteBroker interface, so passing the stub to it crosses a process boundary",
        "does_not_establish": "the identity, privilege or category of the peer that receives the callback"
      },
      {
        "kind": "callback_is_marshalled_to_the_peer",
        "path": "services/src/platform_api_proxy.cpp",
        "commit": "e663b47013d534a56165ab7467fbb3e14bf7172b",
        "sha256": "8fc23c916124bf3dd817fcd7d5d0f19f4b346bdf4855928d58250ec5a6c28a60",
        "line": 47,
        "evidence": "data.WriteRemoteObject(cb->AsObject());",
        "establishes": "the proxy writes the callback object into a Parcel, so the peer receives a usable remote handle to this stub and can send transactions to it",
        "does_not_establish": "whether that peer forwards the handle onward, which is the scenario the missing interface-descriptor check would otherwise constrain"
      }
    ]
